## Project Identity
- **Name:** Etmaam (MVP)
- **Goal:** Automated Tender Qualification & CRM Connector for Saudi Market
- **Core Philosophy:** "Arabic First, Business Ready" (Native RTL)
- **Architecture:** A2UI (Agent-Generated UI) Protocol
- **Competition:** Infratech (20,000 SAR prize)

## Tech Stack (Frozen - Phase 0 Resolution)
- **Frontend:** Next.js 16.1.4 (App Router, Server Actions)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 (Native RTL support via `rtl:` variant)
- **UI Library:** Shadcn/UI (Radix primitives, accessible)
- **Backend/DB:** Supabase (SSR package, Row Level Security)
- **AI:** Vercel AI SDK v4 (Streaming JSON responses)
- **Language:** TypeScript v5.7+ (Strict Mode)
- **i18n:** next-intl (App Router optimized)
- **Icons:** Lucide React (Latest)
- **Font:** IBM Plex Sans Arabic (Google Fonts)

## Coding Standards (The "Stack-Agnostic" Rules)

### 1. Schema First Principle
- **NEVER** write logic without defining the Interface/Type first
- Use Zod schemas for runtime validation
- Generate TypeScript types from Supabase schema

### 2. RTL Native (Critical)
- Every UI component MUST support `dir="rtl"` by default
- Use logical CSS properties (e.g., `ms-2` instead of `ml-2`)
- Use Tailwind v4 logical utilities (`start-`, `end-`, `ms-`, `me-`)
- All icons (arrows, chevrons) must flip automatically in RTL
- Test both `/ar` and `/en` routes

### 3. A2UI Protocol
- UI components should be capable of rendering from JSON streams
- Create `DynamicRenderer` component that maps JSON -> Shadcn Components
- Server Actions return UI-structure JSON, not just raw text

### 4. Error Handling Pattern
- Use "Result Pattern" for Server Actions:
  ```typescript
  return { success: boolean, data?: T, error?: string }
  ```
- Never throw errors directly; wrap in Result type

### 5. Server Components by Default
- Use Server Components unless interactivity is required
- Use Server Actions for data mutations
- Avoid `useEffect` for data fetching; use `await` in Server Components

### 6. Security (Supabase RLS)
- Enable Row Level Security (RLS) on ALL tables
- Use Supabase generated types for TypeScript safety
- Never expose sensitive data in client components

## Directory Structure
```
/app/[locale]/          # Internationalized routes (ar/en)
  /dashboard/           # Main dashboard
  /login/               # Auth pages
/components/
  /ui/                  # Shadcn/UI components
  /a2ui/                # Dynamic renderers for AI content
  /layout/              # Header, Footer, Sidebar
/lib/
  /supabase/            # Typed Supabase clients
  /ai/                  # AI SDK utilities
  /utils/               # Pure utility functions
/types/                 # Shared TypeScript interfaces (Zod schemas preferred)
/actions/                # Server Actions
```

## Naming Conventions
- **Files:** kebab-case (`tender-upload.tsx`)
- **Components:** PascalCase (`TenderUpload`)
- **Functions:** camelCase (`analyzeTender`)
- **Constants:** UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`MAX_FILE_SIZE`)
- **Types/Interfaces:** PascalCase (`TenderData`)

## Testing Rules
- Write tests BEFORE implementation (TDD)
- Use Jest + React Testing Library for components
- Use Playwright for E2E tests
- Mock Supabase client in tests

## Performance Guidelines
- Use `next/image` for all images
- Implement loading skeletons (RTL-aware shimmer)
- Use React Suspense boundaries
- Index database columns: `status`, `created_at`, `user_id`

## Theme System
- **Light Mode:** "Ministry Clean" - White backgrounds, slate text, emerald green accents
- **Dark Mode:** "Midnight Operator" - Deep charcoal (#0f172a), silver text, neon emerald accents
- Use `next-themes` for theme management
- Support system preference detection

## Internationalization
- Default locale: `ar` (Arabic)
- Secondary locale: `en` (English)
- Route structure: `/ar/dashboard`, `/en/dashboard`
- Middleware auto-detects but defaults to Arabic
- All user-facing text MUST use `next-intl` (never hardcode Arabic/English)

## AI Integration
- Use Vercel AI SDK for streaming responses
- AI responses MUST be in Arabic for Arabic locale
- Return structured JSON from AI (not free-form text)
- Implement retry logic for AI API calls

## File Upload Handling
- Support CSV and Excel files
- Handle Arabic encoding properly (UTF-8 with BOM)
- Parse with `papaparse` or `xlsx`
- Sanitize all inputs before database insertion

